.nh
.TH "PB-CONFIG-REPOSITORY-CONNECT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-repository-connect - Connect an HTTPS, SSH, or local Git repository


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config repository connect <url-or-absolute-path> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect an HTTPS, SSH, or local Git repository

.PP
Register an HTTPS, HTTP, SSH URL or absolute local Git path without embedded credentials. Use --name and --branch to select its display name and branch. Machine authentication and explicit file mappings are configured separately.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--branch\fP="main"
	Git branch

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for connect

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	display name


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-repository(1)\fP
